    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0356" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/607</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-08T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 10, 9.25
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am ready and willing to immediately go ahead with the plan of operating the
                    railways which evolved after long negotiations. I have asked Ambassador
                        Morris to complete formalities as
                    early as possible. Myself and service corps are ready to act at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
